 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the navigation law, in relation to base pilotage tariffs at\nSandy Hook, Sands Point and Execution Rocks",
    "basePrintNo": "S9389",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9389-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §88, Nav L",
    "lawSection": "Navigation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9389\n\nSPONSOR: SCARCELLA-SPANTON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the navigation law, in relation to base pilotage tariffs\nat Sandy Hook, Sands Point and Execution Rocks\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation updates and establishes a schedule of base pilotage\ntariff rates for vessels operating in New York waters at Sandy Hook,\nSands Point, and Execution Rocks. The bill provides a structured tariff\nschedule beginning in 2027 and continuing through 2032.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1; Amends section 88 of the navigation law to revise the rate\ntable used to calculate base pilotage tariffs. The bill establishes\nupdated tariff schedules beginning January 1, 2027, and includes incre-\nmental rate adjustments through January 1, 2032.  The rate tables calcu-\nlate tariffs based on pilotage units (P.U.), with different rates\napplied depending on vessel size categories.\n\nSection 2: Provides that the act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPilotage services are critical to the safe navigation of vessels enter-\ning and leaving New York's major ports. State-licensed maritime pilots\nguide ships through complex waterways and ensure safe transit through\nheavily trafficked areas such as Sandy Hook, Sands Point, and Execution\nRocks.\n\nMaintaining appropriate tariff levels for pilotage services is necessary\nto reflect changes in operational costs, industry standards, and econom-\nic conditions. This legislation establishes a structured schedule of\ntariff adjustments over several years, ensuring that rates remain\npredictable and transparent for both pilots and the shipping industry.\n\nBy creating a multi-year schedule of tariff updates, this bill provides\nlong-term stability for maritime operations while supporting the contin-\nued availability of highly skilled pilotage services essential to the\nsafety and efficiency of maritime commerce in New York State.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
